 35S  c  1994Fo04: 159-MeV {+34}S and 167-MeV {+37}Cl beams were produced from  
 35S 2c  the Argonne Tandem Linac Accelerator System (ATLAS). Targets were 1    
 35S 3c  mg/cm{+2} 98.1% enriched {+160}Gd backed by 15 mg/cm{+2} gold. |g rays 
 35S 4c  were detected using the Argonne-Notre Dame BGO |g-ray facility         
 35S 5c  consisting of 12 Compton-suppressed Ge detectors and a 50-element      
 35S 6c  bismuth germanate (BGO) array. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin. Deduced   
 35S 7c  levels. |g|g-coin gates were placed on known |g rays in specific A|?160
 35S 8c  products to select individual reaction channels and identify coincident
 35S 9c  |g rays in light product partners. |g|g-correlation matrices produced  
 35S Ac  with the fold condition 4 |< k |< 9 were found to include most of the  
 35S Bc  events associated with deep inelastic processes.                       
