 35S  c  2014Ay01: {+24}Mg({+14}N,3p){+35}S fusion-evaporation reaction. A      
 35S 2c  40-MeV, 5-pnA {+14}N beam was delivered from the LNL XTU-Tandem        
 35S 3c  accelerator and impinged on 1-mg/cm{+2} thick, 99.7% isotopically      
 35S 4c  enriched {+24}Mg evaporated on an 8-mg/cm{+2} gold layer. |g rays were 
 35S 5c  detected using 4|p-GASP array composed of 40 Compton-suppressed large  
 35S 6c  volume HPGe detectors arranged in seven rings at different angles with 
 35S 7c  respect to beam axis. Events were collected when at least two germanium
 35S 8c  detectors fired in coincidence. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin, |g(|q),  
 35S 9c  |g|g(|q)(ADO). Deduced levels, J, |p, level lifetimes via the Doppler  
 35S Ac  shift attenuation method (DSAM). Compared with large-scale shell model 
 35S Bc  calculations.                                                          
