 35S  c  2021Go09: {+26}Mg+{+18}O->{+44}Ca->2|a+n+{+35}S fusion-evaporation     
 35S 2c  reaction. Exp 1 determined the beam energy for producing high-spin     
 35S 3c  states of {+35}S: an 80-MeV {+18}O beam was delivered from the JAEA    
 35S 4c  tandem accelerator facility and impinged on a 0.5-mg/cm{+2} thick,     
 35S 5c  self-supporting metallic enriched foil of {+26}Mg. |g rays were        
 35S 6c  detected using the GEMINI-II array of 14 Ge detectors with BGO Compton 
 35S 7c  - suppressor shields. The reaction channel was selected by detecting   
 35S 8c  the evaporated charged particles with a 4|p silicon detector. Measured 
 35S 9c  E|g, I|g, |a|g|g-coin, |g|g(|q)(ADO). Exp 2 used the same {+18}O beam  
 35S Ac  energy, the same target, and the same charged-particle detectors as Exp
 35S Bc  1. The beam was delivered from the ALTO-Tandem accelerator facility at 
 35S Cc  IPN Orsay. |g rays were detected using the ORGAM array of 13 Ge        
 35S Dc  detectors based on the EUROGAM with the BGO scintillator for the       
 35S Ec  anti-Compton suppressor. Compared with large-scale shell-model         
 35S Fc  calculations with the SDPF-MSD4 interaction. Also see 2015GoZY,        
 35S Gc  2014GoZZ, 2013GoZW, and 2012IdZZ.                                      
