 35S  c  1972Fr11: 3.50- and 4.00-MeV deuteron beams were produced from the 4-MV
 35S 2c  Van de Graaff accelerator at the Nuclear Research Center of Strasbourg,
 35S 3c  France. Targets were antimony sulphide enriched to 85.6%, 550          
 35S 4c  |mg/cm{+2} on a 0.03 mm molybdenum layer and 150 |mg/cm{+2} on a 0.05  
 35S 5c  mm silver layer. Protons were detected using a surface-barrier annular 
 35S 6c  silicon detector at 180|'. |g rays were detected using a 40 cm{+3}     
 35S 7c  Ge(Li) detector at 0|', 55|' and 90|' with FWHM=3.2 keV at E|g=1.332   
 35S 8c  MeV in the first experiment and a NaI crystal at 0|', 30|', 45|', 60|' 
 35S 9c  and 90|' in the second experiment. Measured E{-p}, E|g, I|g, and       
 35S Ac  p|g(|q)-coin. Deduced 12 levels, J, |g-ray branching ratios, and mixing
 35S Bc  ratios. Deduced T{-1/2} for 7 levels using the Doppler-Shift           
 35S Cc  Attenuation Method (DSAM).                                             
 35S Dc                                                                         
 35S  c  1975VaYG,1972Va07: A 4.72-MeV deuteron beam of 175 nA was provided from
 35S 2c  the Groningen 5 MV Van de Graaff generator. Targets were 80-|mg/cm{+2} 
 35S 3c  Zn{+34}S enriched to 89% evaporated onto 10-|mg/cm{+2} Formva plus     
 35S 4c  10-|mg/cm{+2} carbon. Protons were detected using a 2-mm annular       
 35S 5c  silicon detector. |g rays were detected using a 7.6-cm|*7.6-cm NaI(Tl) 
 35S 6c  detector. Measured E{-p}, E|g, I|g, and p|g(|q)-coin. Deduced levels,  
 35S 7c  J, |g-ray branching ratios, and mixing ratios. Also see 1971VaZG.      
 35S 9c                                                                         
 35S  c  1970Bu18: 2-3.25 MeV deuteron beams were produced from the University  
 35S 2c  of Arizona 5.5 MV Van de Graaff accelerator. Targets were 480          
 35S 3c  {I120}-|mg/cm{+2} Ag{-2}S made by heating 67% enriched {+34}S powder   
 35S 4c  and silver foil. Protons were detected using a 1-mm annular silicon    
 35S 5c  surface barrier detectors and |g rays were detected using a 7.62       
 35S 6c  cm|*7.62 cm NaI(Tl) detector in the angular correlation experiment and 
 35S 7c  a Ge(Li) detector in the lifetime experiment. Measured E{-p}, E|g, I|g,
 35S 8c  and p|g(|q)-coin. Deduced 3 levels, J, |g-ray branching ratios, and    
 35S 9c  mixing ratios. Deduced T{-1/2} for 3 levels using the Doppler-shift    
 35S Ac  attenuation method (DSAM).                                             
 35S Bc                                                                         
 35S  c  2024Co04: A 16-MeV deuteron beam from the John D. Fox Superconducting  
 35S 2c  Linear Accelerator, FSU. Particles were momentum-analyzed by the       
 35S 3c  Super-Enge Split-Pole Spectrograph and identified using a              
 35S 4c  position-sensitive ionization chamber with two anode wires in the      
 35S 5c  isobutane gas (|DE) and a large plastic scintillator (E) at the focal  
 35S 6c  plane. |g rays were detected using a CeBr{-3} Array of five CeBr{-3}   
 35S 7c  detectors. Measured p|g delayed coincidence time spectra and deduced   
 35S 8c  T{-1/2} for the 1991 level of {+35}S.                                  
 35S 9c                                                                         
 35S  c  1971Pr11: A 4.48-MeV deuteron beam was produced from the insulated-core
 35S 2c  transformer tandem accelerator at the Aerospace Research Laboratories  
 35S 3c  (ARL). The target was Ag{-2}S enriched to 85.61% in {+34}S. Protons    
 35S 4c  were detected using a 500 |mm-thick, 50-mm{+2} silicon detector and |g 
 35S 5c  rays were detected using a 1-in.-thick, 1.5-in. in diameter NE111      
 35S 6c  scintillator. Measured p|g-delayed coincidence time spectrum and       
 35S 7c  deduced T{-1/2} for the 1.99-MeV level.                                
 35S 8c                                                                         
 35S  c  1972Go31: A 3.3-MeV deuteron beam was produced from the BNL 3.5-MeV van
 35S 2c  de Graaff facility. The target was Sb{-2}S{-3} enriched to 86% in      
 35S 3c  {+34}S. |g rays were detected using a Ge(Li) detector. Measured        
 35S 4c  E|g=1572.24 {I17} deexiting the first excited state.                   
