 35S  c  1975VaYG,1972Va07: {+37}Cl(d,|a|g){+35}S with a 4.25-MeV deuteron beam 
 35S 2c  of 55 nA from the Groningen 5 MV Van de Graaff generator. The target   
 35S 3c  was a 100 |mg/cm{+2} Co{+37}Cl enriched to 98% evaporated onto         
 35S 4c  10-|mg/cm{+2} Formva plus 10-|mg/cm{+2} carbon. |a particles were      
 35S 5c  detected using a 60-|mm annular silicon detector. |g rays were detected
 35S 6c  using a 120 cm{+3} Ge(Li) detector at 90|'. Measured |s(E{-|a}), E|g,  
 35S 7c  I|g, and |a|g-coin. Deduced levels, |g-ray branching ratios. Also see  
 35S 8c  1971VaZG.                                                              
 35S 9c
 35S  c  1968Te06: {+37}Cl(d,|a|g){+35}S with 3.1-4.6-MeV deuteron beams of 50  
 35S 2c  nA from the Groningen 5-MV Van de Graaff generator. The target was a   
 35S 3c  100-|mg/cm{+2} Co{+37}Cl both of natural {+37}Cl abundance and enriched
 35S 4c  to 93% evaporated onto 10-|mg/cm{+2} Formva plus 10-|mg/cm{+2} carbon. 
 35S 5c  |a particles were detected using an annular solid-state detector at    
 35S 6c  168-173|'. |g rays were detected using a 3 in. by 3 in. NaI(Tl)        
 35S 7c  scintillator at 55|'. Measured |s(E{-|a}), E|g, and |a|g-coin. Deduced 
 35S 8c  levels.                                                                
 35S  c  1955Pa54: {+37}Cl(d,|a){+35}S with 3.0, 5.6, 6.0, 7.0, and 7.5-MeV     
 35S 2c  deuteron beams from the MIT-ONR electrostatic generator. Targets were  
 35S 3c  80- and 300-|mg/cm{+2} Barium chloride (75.4% {+35}Cl, 24.6% {+37}Cl)  
 35S 4c  evaporated onto formvar films on a gold layer. Charged reaction        
 35S 5c  products emitted at 90|' were magnetically analyzed by a broad-range   
 35S 6c  spectrograph. Measured |s(E{-|a}). Deduced levels.                     
