 35S  c  {+37}Cl->{+35}S+1p1n from J|p=3/2+ {+37}Cl ground state.               
 35S  c  1975Gu15: A 40.2-MeV proton beam was produced from the Michigan State  
 35S 2c  University cyclotron. The target was 55 |mg/cm{+2} NaCl with 97%       
 35S 3c  enriched {+37}Cl made by evaporation of the salt onto a 30-|mg/cm{+2}  
 35S 4c  carbon backing. The reaction products were detected using a            
 35S 5c  wire-counter plastic-scintillator in the focal plane of an Enge        
 35S 6c  split-pole spectrograph with FWHM=30 keV. Measured |s(E({+3}He),|q).   
 35S 7c  Deduced levels, L from zero-range DWUCK-DWBA analysis of the measured  
 35S 8c  |s(|q).                                                                
 35S  c  1971Vi02: A 40-MeV proton beam was produced from the Grenoble variable 
 35S 2c  energy cyclotron at intensities of 20-200 nA depending on the          
 35S 3c  scattering angle with a 90-keV energy resolution. The target was       
 35S 4c  natural purified chlorine gas 100 mm in diameter and 25 mm in height.  
 35S 5c  The reaction particles were detected using two separate counter        
 35S 6c  telescopes with each consisting of a 200|mm phosphorous-drifted silicon
 35S 7c  |DE detector, a 2-mm lithium-drifted silicon E detector and a 3-mm     
 35S 8c  lithium-drifted silicon E-reject detector with FWHM=180 keV for {+3}He.
 35S 9c  Measured |s(E({+3}He),|q). Deduced L for {+35}S ground state from      
 35S Ac  zero-range Nelson-DWBA analysis of the measured |s(|q).                
